### TITLE ###
Fmt_RejectsShellFlag
### INPUT ###
### ARGS ###
fmt
--check
--shell
### STDOUT ###
exit 1
### STDERR ###
--shell only applies when running a Rad script; "fmt" is a built-in rad command.

Formats Rad scripts.

Rewrites each script in place into Rad's canonical style. Use --stdout to
preview without writing, or --check to verify formatting (e.g. in CI).

Usage:
  rad fmt [paths...] [OPTIONS]

Arguments:
      --paths [strs...]   Paths of Rad scripts to format.
      --stdout            Print formatted output to stdout instead of writing files. Excludes: check
      --check             Don't write; exit non-zero if any file isn't formatted.

Global options:
  -h, --help          Print usage string.
  -i, --interactive   Interactively prompt for script args not already provided, then run.
      --color mode    Control output colorization. Valid values: [auto, always, never] (default auto)
  -q, --quiet         Suppresses some output.
### EXIT ###
1

