### TITLE ###
Docs_RejectsMockResponse
### INPUT ###
### ARGS ###
docs
--mock-response
x:y
### STDERR ###
--mock-response only applies when running a Rad script; "docs" is a built-in rad command.

Prints Rad's documentation - a page, the full corpus, or an error code.

Examples:
> rad docs
Lists every documentation topic.

> rad docs guide/basics
Prints the 'basics' guide page.

> rad docs reference/functions
Prints the function reference.

> rad docs len
Prints the doc for the 'len' built-in function.

> rad docs all
Prints the entire documentation corpus (the same set as llms-full.txt).

> rad docs RAD10001
Explains error code RAD10001.

> rad docs guide/basics --web
Opens the page on the documentation website instead of printing.

Usage:
  rad docs [topic] [OPTIONS]

Arguments:
      --topic str   The topic to print: a page slug (e.g. 'guide/basics'), an error code (e.g. 'RAD10001'), or 'all'.
  -w, --web         Open the documentation website in a browser instead of printing.
      --raw         Force raw markdown output (no terminal rendering). Excludes: render
      --render      Force terminal-rendered output, even when piped.

Global options:
  -h, --help          Print usage string.
  -i, --interactive   Interactively prompt for script args not already provided, then run.
      --color mode    Control output colorization. Valid values: [auto, always, never] (default auto)
  -q, --quiet         Suppresses some output.
### EXIT ###
1

